1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,832
Imagine the ocean thirteen million years ago. No ice

2
00:00:03,832 --> 00:00:07,664
at the poles, warmer seas, and the water full

3
00:00:07,664 --> 00:00:08,516
of life.

4
00:00:08,866 --> 00:00:12,123
Now imagine you're swimming there, and something enormous passes

5
00:00:12,123 --> 00:00:15,380
beneath you. Not a shark. Not a whale you'd

6
00:00:15,380 --> 00:00:18,637
recognize. Something built like a sperm whale, but bigger,

7
00:00:18,637 --> 00:00:21,894
and with a mouth that looks like it was

8
00:00:21,894 --> 00:00:23,704
designed to end arguments quickly.

9
00:00:24,054 --> 00:00:27,134
Its name was Livyatan. And it might have been

10
00:00:27,134 --> 00:00:30,214
one of the most dangerous animals the ocean has

11
00:00:30,214 --> 00:00:30,898
ever produced.

12
00:00:31,248 --> 00:00:34,379
Today we're going back about thirteen million years, to

13
00:00:34,379 --> 00:00:37,510
the Miocene epoch, to meet an animal that paleontologists

14
00:00:37,510 --> 00:00:40,642
think sat at the very top of its ecosystem.

15
00:00:40,642 --> 00:00:43,773
We'll look at what it was, how big it

16
00:00:43,773 --> 00:00:46,556
got, what it hunted, and why it disappeared.

17
00:00:46,906 --> 00:00:50,254
Let's start with the name, because it's a bit

18
00:00:50,254 --> 00:00:53,603
of a story. The scientific name is Livyatan melvillei.

19
00:00:53,603 --> 00:00:56,951
The first part comes from the Hebrew word "Leviathan,"

20
00:00:56,951 --> 00:00:59,183
a sea monster from ancient texts.

21
00:00:59,533 --> 00:01:02,535
The second part honors Herman Melville, the author of

22
00:01:02,535 --> 00:01:05,537
Moby-Dick. So the animal is named after a sea

23
00:01:05,537 --> 00:01:08,206
monster and the man who wrote about one.

24
00:01:08,556 --> 00:01:12,169
Let's talk size, because this is where it gets

25
00:01:12,169 --> 00:01:15,781
hard to picture. Estimates for Livyatan put its length

26
00:01:15,781 --> 00:01:19,394
somewhere between about 13 and 17 meters, roughly 43

27
00:01:19,394 --> 00:01:20,598
to 56 feet.

28
00:01:20,948 --> 00:01:24,041
For comparison, a standard American school bus is around

29
00:01:24,041 --> 00:01:27,133
12 meters (about 40 feet) long. So Livyatan was

30
00:01:27,133 --> 00:01:30,226
at least as long as a school bus, and

31
00:01:30,226 --> 00:01:33,318
possibly longer than a bus with another car attached

32
00:01:33,318 --> 00:01:34,349
